{"event":"pre_tool","ts":1772871831934,"session":"ralph-20260307-082232","tool":"task","args":"{\"agent_type\": \"ralph.malph-scout\", \"description\": \"Scout PR 2901 diff\", \"prompt\": \"You are scouting PR #2901 for DOC-3141 (Tag attribute editor validation) on branch `ralph/doc-3141`.\\n\\n**Issue summary:** Add missing editor-level validation across all tag definitions. The implementation should be generic and reusable (like required attribute validation), not custom per-tag. Two revisions were done — first added 3 generic rules (validateDuplicateAttributes, validateEmptyRequiredAttributeValue, validatePositionalAttributeAllowedValues), second added 2 more (validateMutuallyExclusiveAttributes, validateAttributeDependency) plus dataType on all attributes.\\n\\n**Your tasks:**\\n1. Find PR #2901 (branch: ralph/doc-3141, target: main)\\n2. Run `git diff main...ralph/doc-3141` to identify all changed files\\n3. Map each change to the extension's architectural patterns (see .github/copilot-instructions.md)\\n4. Run build validation: `npm run compile`, `npm run lint:ci`, `npm run test:xvfb`\\n5. Write your scout report to `.ralph/tasks/DOC-3141/artifacts/malph-scout/output.md`\\n6. Write status to `.ralph/tasks/DOC-3141/artifacts/malph-scout/status.json`\\n\\nThe artifacts directory exists at `.ralph/tasks/DOC-3141/artifacts/` — create the `malph-scout/` subdirectory.\\n\\nStatus JSON format:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"scouted\\\" | \\\"build-broken\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"blocked\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"<brief summary of findings>\\\",\\n  \\\"buildResult\\\": \\\"pass\\\" | \\\"fail\\\",\\n  \\\"testResult\\\": \\\"pass\\\" | \\\"fail\\\",\\n  \\\"lintResult\\\": \\\"pass\\\" | \\\"fail\\\",\\n  \\\"changedFiles\\\": <count>,\\n  \\\"prId\\\": 2901\\n}\\n```\", \"mode\": \"sync\"}"}
