{"event":"pre_tool","ts":1772872815303,"session":"ralph-20260307-082232","tool":"jira-kentico-jira_add_comment","args":"{\"body\": \"h2. 🦇 Review Panel Verdict: APPROVED\\n\\n*Panel:* 3 reviewers (Opus 4.6, GPT 5.4, Gemini Pro)\\n*Scout:* Build PASS · Lint PASS · 452 tests PASS\\n\\nh3. Reviewer Verdicts\\n|| Reviewer || Verdict || Findings ||\\n| malph-reviewer-opus | ✅ approved | 2 suggestions |\\n| malph-reviewer-gpt | ✅ approved | 4 suggestions |\\n| malph-reviewer-gemini | ✅ approved | 3 suggestions |\\n\\nh3. Aggregated Findings\\n\\nAll findings are *suggestions* (non-blocking). No critical or style issues found.\\n\\nh4. Suggestions\\n\\n* *[SUG-001]* {{src/definitions/tags/block/card/diagnostics/imageAttrConflict.ts}} — Orphaned dead code file. The custom {{validateCardIconImageConflict}} rule was replaced by declarative {{mutuallyExclusiveWith}}, but the file was not deleted. _(flagged by: opus, gpt, gemini)_\\n* *[SUG-002]* {{src/logic/diagnostics/tags/rules/validateDuplicateAttributes.rule.ts:3}} — Unused import {{findTagAttributeNameRange}} from {{../helpers}}. Only {{createTagDiagnostic}} is used. _(flagged by: gpt, gemini)_\\n* *[SUG-003]* {{src/logic/diagnostics/tags/rules/validateDuplicateAttributes.rule.ts:27}} — Duplicate detection regex may false-positive on attribute values containing {{=}} inside quoted strings (e.g. {{title=\\\"lang=test\\\"}}). Low probability in practice. _(flagged by: gpt, gemini)_\\n* *[SUG-004]* Three rule files import {{TagValidationContext}} alongside {{TagValidationRuleFn}} but only use the function type directly. _(flagged by: opus)_\\n* *[SUG-005]* {{src/logic/diagnostics/tags/rules/validateEmptyRequiredAttributeValue.rule.ts:28}} — Inconsistent diagnostic message format: positional attributes missing the word \\\"attribute\\\" and quotes around the name. _(flagged by: gpt)_\\n\\nh3. Summary\\n\\nClean work. The definition-driven approach is well-executed — five new generic validation rules, all properly registered and tested. The architecture follows established patterns (declarative definitions consumed by centralized providers). The {{mutuallyExclusiveWith}} and {{dependsOn}} additions are particularly elegant. All findings are cosmetic cleanup items. The night approves.\"}"}
